          %p
            There are many consequences of having identity types between types in the dependent type theory. One such example is that any time one uses an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+types"} equivalence of types
            in a definition, such as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+Tarski+universes"} weak Tarski universes
            or typal large recursion principles for inductive types, one can instead use identity types between types in the definition. In addition, one can add
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalence"} univalence
            to the dependent type theory itself, which makes the identity types between types and equivalence types coincide with each other.
          %h4#univalence_axiom  Univalence axiom
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalence+axiom"} univalence axiom
            states that the function
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} idtoequiv
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo =
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{idtoequiv}(A, B):(A = B) \to (A \simeq B)
          %p inductively defined by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} idtoequiv
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} refl
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} id
                    %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{idtoequiv}(A, A, \mathrm{refl}(A)) \coloneqq \mathrm{id}_A
          %p
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+types"} equivalence of types
            for all types
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isEquiv
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} idtoequiv
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{isEquiv}(\mathrm{idtoequiv}(A, B))
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} id
                    %mi A
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi λ
                  %mi x
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo .
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{id}_A \coloneqq \lambda x:A.x
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+function"} identity function
            on the type
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/impredicative+polymorphism"} impredicative polymorphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ctx
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ua
                      %mo :
                      %mi Π
                      %mi A
                      %mo .
                      %mi Π
                      %mi B
                      %mo .
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isEquiv
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi λ
                      %mi p
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo =
                      %mi B
                      %mo .
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} idtoequiv
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                      %mo ,
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \; \mathrm{ctx}}{\Gamma \vdash \mathrm{ua}:\Pi A.\Pi B.\mathrm{isEquiv}(\lambda p:A = B.\mathrm{idtoequiv}(A, B, p))}
          %p
            Unlike the other presentation of dependent type theory in terms of universes, in this presentation of dependent type theory with a type judgment and type variables, it
            %em is consistent
            to assume both the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalence+axiom"} univalence axiom
            and an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+set+truncation"} axiom of set truncation
            like
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/UIP"} UIP
            or
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+K"} axiom K
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+type"} circle type
          %h4#large_recursion_principles Large recursion principles
          %p
            In the usual dependent type theory without type variables, large recursion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inductive+types"} inductive types
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+inductive+types"} higher inductive types
            is usually expressed in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+types"} equivalences
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transport"} transport
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+type"} circle type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
            usually states that given a type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/autoequivalence"} autoequivalence
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e:A \simeq A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ⊢
                  %msubsup
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} lrec
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 1
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:S^1 \vdash \mathrm{lrec}_{S^1}^{A, e}(x)
            such that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} lrec
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 1
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} base
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≡
                  %mi A
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                  %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} and
                  %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                  %msubsup
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} tr
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 1
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} lrec
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 1
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                          %mo ,
                          %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} base
                  %mo ,
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} base
                  %mo ,
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} loop
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≡
                  %mi e
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{lrec}_{S^1}^{A, e}(\mathrm{base}) \equiv A \; \mathrm{type} \quad \mathrm{and} \quad \mathrm{tr}_{S^1}^{\mathrm{lrec}_{S^1}^{A, e}}(\mathrm{base}, \mathrm{base}, \mathrm{loop}) \equiv e:A \simeq A
          %p
            However, with type variables, instead of using equivalences and transport, one can instead use
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+type#IdentityTypesBetweenTypes"} identity types between types
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+on+identifications"} action on identifications
            for type families. For example, an alternative strict large recursion principle of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+type"} circle type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
            states that given a type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identification"} identification
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo =
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p:A = A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ⊢
                  %msubsup
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} lrec
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 1
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:S^1 \vdash \mathrm{lrec}_{S^1}^{A, p}(x)
            such that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} lrec
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 1
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} base
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≡
                  %mi A
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                  %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} and
                  %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                  %msubsup
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ap
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 1
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} lrec
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 1
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                          %mo ,
                          %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} base
                  %mo ,
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} base
                  %mo ,
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} loop
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≡
                  %mi p
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo =
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{lrec}_{S^1}^{A, p}(\mathrm{base}) \equiv A \; \mathrm{type} \quad \mathrm{and} \quad \mathrm{ap}_{S^1}^{\mathrm{lrec}_{S^1}^{A, p}}(\mathrm{base}, \mathrm{base}, \mathrm{loop}) \equiv p:A = A
          %p
            In addition, traditionally without type variables, there are strict and weak versions of large recursion principles: the strict large recursion principles use
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/judgmental+equality"} judgmental equality
            between types for the computation and uniqueness rules, while the weak large recursion principles use
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalences+of+types"} equivalences of types
            for the computation and uniqueness rules. For example, the strict large recursion principle for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+of+booleans"} type of booleans
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝟚
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{2}
            says that given types
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo :
                  %mi 𝟚
                  %mo ⊢
                  %msubsup
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} lrec
                    %mi 𝟚
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:\mathbb{2} \vdash \mathrm{lrec}_\mathbb{2}^{A, B}(x)
            such that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} lrec
                    %mi 𝟚
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≡
                  %mi A
                  %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} and
                  %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                  %msubsup
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} lrec
                    %mi 𝟚
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≡
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{lrec}_\mathbb{2}^{A, B}(0) \equiv A \quad \mathrm{and} \quad \mathrm{lrec}_\mathbb{2}^{A, B}(1) \equiv B
          %p
            and the weak large recursion principle for the type of booleans says that the type family above comes with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalences+of+types"} equivalences of types
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} l
                  %msubsup
                    %mi β
                    %mi 𝟚
                    %mi A
                  %mo :
                  %msubsup
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} lrec
                    %mi 𝟚
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi A
                  %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} and
                  %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} l
                  %msubsup
                    %mi β
                    %mi 𝟚
                    %mi B
                  %mo :
                  %msubsup
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} lrec
                    %mi 𝟚
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{l}\beta_\mathbb{2}^{A}:\mathrm{lrec}_\mathbb{2}^{A, B}(0) \simeq A \quad \mathrm{and} \quad \mathrm{l}\beta_\mathbb{2}^{B}:\mathrm{lrec}_\mathbb{2}^{A, B}(1) \simeq B
          %p
            However, with type variables and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+type#IdentityTypesBetweenTypes"} identity types between types
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} l
                  %msubsup
                    %mi β
                    %mi 𝟚
                    %mi A
                  %mo :
                  %msubsup
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} lrec
                    %mi 𝟚
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi A
                  %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} and
                  %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} l
                  %msubsup
                    %mi β
                    %mi 𝟚
                    %mi B
                  %mo :
                  %msubsup
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} lrec
                    %mi 𝟚
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{l}\beta_\mathbb{2}^{A}:\mathrm{lrec}_\mathbb{2}^{A, B}(0) = A \quad \mathrm{and} \quad \mathrm{l}\beta_\mathbb{2}^{B}:\mathrm{lrec}_\mathbb{2}^{A, B}(1) = B
          %p This third notion of weak large recursion in dependent type theory with a single type judgment and type variables parallels the usual notion of weak large recursion in the other formulation of dependent type theory involving a hierarchy of universes, where large recursion simply means the usual recursion principle into one of the predefined universes in the hierarchy.
          %h3#large_recursion_principles_of_recursive_inductive_types Large recursion principles of recursive inductive types
          %p
            Independently of the consequences of having
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+type#IdentityTypesBetweenTypes"} identity types between types
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers+type"} natural numbers type
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/W-types"} W-types
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localizations+of+a+type"} localizations of a type
          %p
            For example, the usual recursion principle for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers+type"} natural numbers type
            is given by the following: given
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                a type
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %li
              %p
                an element
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mn 0
                      %mo :
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_0:C
            %li
              %p
                a family of elements
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo :
                      %mi ℕ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi C
                      %mo ⊢
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mi s
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n:\mathbb{N}, x:C \vdash c_s(n, x):C
          %p one can construct a family of elements
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo :
                  %mi ℕ
                  %mo ⊢
                  %msubsup
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} rec
                    %mi ℕ
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n:\mathbb{N} \vdash \mathrm{rec}_\mathbb{N}^{C, c_0, c_s}(n):C
          %p such that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} rec
                    %mi ℕ
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≡
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 0
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{rec}_\mathbb{N}^{C, c_0, c_s}(0) \equiv c_0:C
          %p and
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo :
                  %mi ℕ
                  %mo ⊢
                  %msubsup
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} rec
                    %mi ℕ
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≡
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo ,
                  %msubsup
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} rec
                    %mi ℕ
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n:\mathbb{N} \vdash \mathrm{rec}_\mathbb{N}^{C, c_0, c_s}(s(n)) \equiv c_s(n, \mathrm{rec}_\mathbb{N}^{C, c_0, c_s}(n):C
          %p
            In the other formulation of dependent type theory in terms of a hierarchy of universes and no type judgment, large recursion of the natural numbers is simply the recursion principle for a universe
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i
            in the hierarchy: given
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                a universe
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            %li
              %p
                an type
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mn 0
                      %mo :
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_0:U
            %li
              %p
                a family of elements
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo :
                      %mi ℕ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi X
                      %mo :
                      %mi U
                      %mo ⊢
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mi s
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo ,
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n:\mathbb{N}, X:U \vdash T_s(n, X):U
          %p one can construct a family of elements
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo :
                  %mi ℕ
                  %mo ⊢
                  %msubsup
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} rec
                    %mi ℕ
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n:\mathbb{N} \vdash \mathrm{rec}_\mathbb{N}^{U, T_0, T_s}(n):U
          %p such that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} rec
                    %mi ℕ
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≡
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mn 0
                  %mo :
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{rec}_\mathbb{N}^{U, T_0, T_s}(0) \equiv T_0:U
          %p and
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo :
                  %mi ℕ
                  %mo ⊢
                  %msubsup
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} rec
                    %mi ℕ
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≡
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo ,
                  %msubsup
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} rec
                    %mi ℕ
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n:\mathbb{N} \vdash \mathrm{rec}_\mathbb{N}^{U, T_0, T_s}(s(n)) \equiv T_s(n, \mathrm{rec}_\mathbb{N}^{U, T_0, T_s}(n):U
          %p
            However, in dependent type theory with a single type judgment, the universe
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            is not needed and in fact non-existent. Translating the large recursion principle into type judgments, we get the following: given
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                a type
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mn 0
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_0 \; \mathrm{type}
            %li
              %p
                a family of types
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo :
                      %mi ℕ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi X
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                      %mo ⊢
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mi s
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo ,
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n:\mathbb{N}, X \; \mathrm{type} \vdash T_s(n, X) \; \mathrm{type}
          %p one can construct a family of types
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo :
                  %mi ℕ
                  %mo ⊢
                  %msubsup
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} rec
                    %mi ℕ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n:\mathbb{N} \vdash \mathrm{rec}_\mathbb{N}^{T_0, T_s}(n) \; \mathrm{type}
          %p such that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} rec
                    %mi ℕ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≡
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mn 0
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{rec}_\mathbb{N}^{T_0, T_s}(0) \equiv T_0 \; \mathrm{type}
          %p and
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo :
                  %mi ℕ
                  %mo ⊢
                  %msubsup
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} rec
                    %mi ℕ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≡
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo ,
                  %msubsup
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} rec
                    %mi ℕ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n:\mathbb{N} \vdash \mathrm{rec}_\mathbb{N}^{T_0, T_s}(s(n)) \equiv T_s(n, \mathrm{rec}_\mathbb{N}^{T_0, T_s}(n)) \; \mathrm{type}
          %p
            It is clear that type variables are needed, since otherwise the second requirement in the large recursion principle that we have a family of types
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo :
                  %mi ℕ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                  %mo ⊢
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n:\mathbb{N}, X \; \mathrm{type} \vdash T_s(n, X) \; \mathrm{type}
            will not be possible.
          %p
            Similar requirements of type variables apply to the large recursion principles of more general recursive inductive types like
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/W-types"} W-types
          %h2#type_family_variables Type family variables
          %h3#with_function_types With function types
          %p
            Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            with
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+variables"} type variables
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+sum+types"} dependent sum types
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+types"} identity types
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+types"} function types
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and functions to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            are equivalent to each other:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                By the inference rules of
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+sum+types"} dependent sum types
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:A \vdash B(x)
                is equivalently a type
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo :
                          %mi A
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_{x:A} B(x)
                with a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_A
                to
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %li
              %p
                Similarly, a type
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                with a function
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi B
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:B \to A
                is equivalently a type family
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo :
                        %mi A
                        %mo ⊢
                        %msub
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                          %mrow
                            %mi y
                            %mo :
                            %mi B
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %msub
                          %mo =
                          %mi A
                        %mi y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:A \vdash \sum_{y:B} f(x) =_A y
          %p
            If the type theory is formulated using a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hierarchy+of+universes"} hierarchy of universes
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A:U_i
            that the above operations form an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+types"} equivalence of types
            between the following types:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                        %mo :
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                    %mo )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A \to U_i) \simeq \left(\sum_{B:U_i} B \to A\right)
          %p
            As a result, a
            %em type family variable
            or a
            %em variable of type families
            simply consists of a type variable and a term variable of a function type:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                  %mo ,
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Gamma, B \; \mathrm{type}, f:B \to A, \Delta)
          %h3#with_type_telescopes With type telescopes
          %p
            On the other hand, if the dependent type theory does not have
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+types"} function types
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+homotopy+type+theory"} geometric homotopy type theory
            as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"} internal logic
            of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"}
                Grothendieck
                = succeed "-topos" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+telescopes"} type telescopes
            to the theory. Via telescopes, we have, for each type
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/judgment"} judgment
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \; \mathrm{type} / (x:A)
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x:A)
            is the telescope consisting of the judgment
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:A
          %p
            With type telescopes, there
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inference+rules"} inference rules
            which mimic the inference rules for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+types"} function types
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to U_i
            for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+universe"} type universe
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i
            are derivable from the inference rules for telescopes:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi λ
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo .
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma, x:A \vdash B(x) \; \mathrm{type}}{\Gamma \vdash \lambda x:A.B(x) \; \mathrm{type} / (x:A)}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi B
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash B \; \mathrm{type} / (x:A)}{\Gamma, x:A \vdash B(x) \; \mathrm{type}}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≡
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi λ
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo .
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma, x:A \vdash B(x) \; \mathrm{type}}{\Gamma, x:A \vdash B(x) \equiv (\lambda x:A.B(x))(x) \; \mathrm{type}}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi B
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi B
                      %mo ≡
                      %mi λ
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo .
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash B \; \mathrm{type} / (x:A)}{\Gamma \vdash B \equiv \lambda x:A.B(x) \; \mathrm{type} / (x:A)}
          %p
            Then we have additional context forming rules that says that given a type judgment
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \; \mathrm{type}
            in context
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \; \mathrm{type} / (x:A)
            the context:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ctx
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ctx
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \; \mathrm{ctx} \quad \Gamma \vdash A \; \mathrm{type}}{(\Gamma, B \; \mathrm{type} / (x:A)) \; \mathrm{ctx}}
          %p
            In addition, the judgment
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo :
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b : B / (x:A)
            behaves as a dependent function, and we also have
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inference+rules"} inference rules
            which mimic the inference rules for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+function+types"} dependent function types
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x:A) \to B(x)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi λ
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo .
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi λ
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo .
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma, x:A \vdash B(x) \; \mathrm{type} \quad \Gamma, x:A \vdash b(x):B(x)}{\Gamma \vdash \lambda x:A.b(x) : \lambda x:A.B(x) / (x:A)}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi B
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} at
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi b
                      %mo :
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash B \; \mathrm{type} \; \mathrm{at} \; A \quad \Gamma \vdash b: B / (x:A)}{\Gamma, x:A \vdash b(x):B(x)}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≡
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi λ
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo .
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma, x:A \vdash B(x) \; \mathrm{type} \quad \Gamma, x:A \vdash b(x):B(x)}{\Gamma \vdash b(x) \equiv (\lambda x:A.b(x))(x):B(x)}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi B
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} at
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi b
                      %mo :
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi b
                      %mo ≡
                      %mi λ
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo .
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash B \; \mathrm{type} \; \mathrm{at} \; A \quad \Gamma \vdash b: B / (x:A)}{\Gamma \vdash b \equiv \lambda x:A.b(x) : B / (x:A)}
          %p
            Then we have additional context forming rules that says that given the judgment
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \; \mathrm{type} / (x:A)
            in context
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo :
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b : B / (x:A)
            to the context:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ctx
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi B
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} at
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo :
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ctx
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \; \mathrm{ctx} \quad \Gamma \vdash B \; \mathrm{type} \; \mathrm{at} \; A}{(\Gamma, b : B  / (x:A)) \; \mathrm{ctx}}
          %p
            Collectively, the additions of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+telescopes"} type telescopes
            to the dependent type theory behave as if it is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modal+type+theory"} modal type theory
            whose mode theory is given by the original
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            and represents, for an
            = succeed "-topos" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C2%29-category"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,2)
              \-category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"}
              slice
              = succeed "-toposes" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
